 keepalive 2.0.0 · help

 ↑ ↓    choose how long
 enter  start
 ?      this help
 q      quit
 a      simulate activity
 d      keep the display on
 b      stop at a battery level
 k      tap Shift with activity

 Simulate activity moves the pointer in
 small arcs (up to about 130 px) and
 back to where it was, once you have
 been idle for a while, so Teams and
 Slack keep showing you as Active.
 It pauses while you use the computer
 or the screen is locked; "keepalive
 doctor" checks that it works here.
 Logs: off; start with --log to write
 /home/u/.cache/keepalive/keepalive.log

 ? or esc close
